WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.430
Hold a light filter, the
kind used in some sunglasses,

2
00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.860
up to a lamp.

3
00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:08.000
An ideal filter lets
half the light through.

4
00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:11.070
Add a second filter and slowly turn it.

5
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.690
At a quarter turn, the light is gone.

6
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:14.830
Keep turning.

7
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.620
By half a turn, it is bright again.

8
00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:19.930
Sound has no trick like this.

9
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.400
Turning a filter never blocks it.

10
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:25.340
So what does that difference
tell us about light?

11
00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:28.550
In this mission, you'll shake
a rope through a narrow slot,

12
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.820
and see which shakes get through.

13
00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:35.190
Then you'll see what it means for a
wave to vibrate in just one plane.

14
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:39.390
Your mission: explain what this
filter trick tells us about light.
